  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), STECS Max with the right Space Throttle Grip (STG-R_03) seen from the left rear and above: grip thumb face (left side of the right-hand grip), STEM panel on the left, STECS base panel and ATEM module in the foreground; grip front with the main trigger hidden",
  "mappingSource": "catalog vkb.json (no inputs: right Max PID and numbering not found; parts copied from vkb-stecs-stg-max-left). Grip control names and spots from VKB's \"STECS Space Throttle RH\" template v1.0 by UntoldForce (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0808/7827/2731/files/VKB-STECS-SpaceThrottleGrip-RH-v1.0.pdf: Pointer Hat, HAT1, Speed Lim, H1, B1, B2, H2, Main Trigger, base Mode 1-5 / START / SYS), ATEM template v1.0 (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0808/7827/2731/files/VKB-STECS-ATEM-v1.0.pdf) and STEM template v1.0 (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0808/7827/2731/files/VKB-STECS-STEM-v1.0_1d344eed-eb3d-4326-bff2-541f981d4e2a.pdf), linked on https://vkbsimcontrollers.com/pages/downloads; printed labels on the grip, STEM and ATEM",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "same part-to-control matching as the left Max draft (p09 vkb-stecs-stg-max-left): hat.mic = HAT1, hat.1 = SPEED LIM, hat.2 = Pointer hat on the stalk, hat.3 = H1, hat.4 = H2, button.1 = B1, button.3 = B2, button.2 = main trigger (hidden front). slider.1/slider.2: the two analog axes (template: Brake, Laser) have no lines on the template; the big ribbed paddle on the grip end is one of them - which one is a guess (candidate), the other is not identified. The throttle axis itself and STG x/y have no catalog part. ATEM is one catalog part toggle.5 (up/down, copied from the left Max: SAFE = up, ARMED = down); marker on the SAFE pad, ARMED is the lower left pad at 0.704 0.769. The ATEM PUSH multi-stick is both hat.5 and encoder.3. MODE 1-5 are positions of the white base rotary (one spot). SYS = the round lit base button (medium, as in the left draft).",
